brief:
The person tagged the bot in a reply. The post they tagged it in says:
you have to @buildthis.bisks.net - please implement what norvid described

The thread it's replying to, oldest first (this is the context "this" refers to):
@norvid-studies.bsky.social: I want to create a grid that's all mutuals first reply to every other mutual. what's the best, easiest and fastest way to do this
@bisks.net: @buildthis.bisks.net
@buildthis.bisks.net: built mootrace: point it at a handle and it downloads every mutual's whole repo to find who broke the ice first with every other mutual — a full grid, straight from @norvid-studies' ask.

built it 🎉 — https://mootrace.bisks.net

(give the deploy a minute to go live)
@norvid-studies.bsky.social: okay, this is cool so please save this version without replacing it, but the ask was actually something else: not a site that shows who replied first, [the account], or their mutual; INSTEAD;

1. for a given account, create a list of their 40 top mutuals (the ones who reply to them the most) 
2.
@norvid-studies.bsky.social: now generate the entire grid of the FIRST TIME each of those mutuals replied to each of the others (both of their first replies). eg if I'm followed by Abel and Buildbisks, I want to be able to see Abel's first reply to buildbisks ever, and buildbisks first reply to abel ever. please include the
@norvid-studies.bsky.social: text in the grid, as well as the link to the tweet. so that the grid shows the entirety of the mutuals first interactions with each other, each one's first message for each pair, among all top mutuals for whom interactions exist
